@startuml login-sequence
title Login Flow – PKCE OAuth2 with AWS Cognito

skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam participantBorderRadius 6

actor User
participant "Browser\nVue SPA\n(chat.example.com)" as Vue #fff2cc
participant "AWS Cognito\nHosted UI\n+ Token endpoint" as Cognito #f8cecc
participant "FastAPI\nECS Fargate\n(chat-api)" as API #d5e8d4
participant "PostgreSQL\nchatapi database" as RDS #f5f5f5

== ① Initiate Login ==

User -> Vue : Click Login (or route guard fires)

== ② PKCE Generation ==

note over Vue
  pkce.ts:
  1. Generate code_verifier (32 random bytes, base64url)
  2. code_challenge = base64url(SHA-256(verifier))
  3. Store verifier → sessionStorage[pkce_verifier]
end note

== ③ Cognito Auth ==

Vue -> Cognito : HTTP 302 → Cognito Hosted UI\n?response_type=code&client_id=...\n&code_challenge=SHA256(verifier)&code_challenge_method=S256\n&scope=openid+email+profile&redirect_uri=.../callback

User -> Cognito : Enter username + password

note over Cognito
  Cognito validates credentials
  (password policy, prevent-user-existence-errors)
end note

Cognito -> Vue : HTTP 302 → /callback?code=AUTH_CODE

== ④ Token Exchange ==

note over Vue
  CallbackView.vue:
  Extract code from URL query string
  → call auth.handleCallback(code)
end note

Vue -> Cognito : POST /oauth2/token\ngrant_type=authorization_code\ncode=AUTH_CODE + code_verifier=STORED_VERIFIER\nclient_id + redirect_uri

note over Cognito
  Cognito verifies:
  SHA-256(code_verifier) == code_challenge
  Issues tokens (RS256 signed)
end note

Cognito -> Vue : 200 OK { id_token: JWT, access_token, refresh_token }\n(id_token: 1 h, refresh_token: 30 d)

note over Vue
  auth.ts:
  localStorage.setItem('id_token', jwt)
  sessionStorage.removeItem('pkce_verifier')
  router.push('/')  →  ChatView loads
end note

== ⑤ Authenticated Request ==

note over Vue : (Subsequent API calls — every request)

Vue -> API : GET /api/v1/conversations\nAuthorization: Bearer <id_token JWT>

note over API
  dependencies.py → security.py:
  1. Extract JWT from Bearer header
  2. Decode header → get kid
  3. Fetch JWKS from Cognito (cached in-process)
  4. Find matching public key by kid
  5. Verify RS256 signature
  6. Validate: aud=CLIENT_ID, iat≤now, exp>now
  7. Extract sub claim (user ID)
end note

API -> RDS : SELECT * FROM conversations\nWHERE user_sub = {sub} ORDER BY updated_at DESC
RDS -> API : [{ id, title, created_at, updated_at }, ...]
API -> Vue : 200 OK — ConversationList JSON

note over Vue, API
  On token expiry (1 h) the axios interceptor catches 401
  → auth.logout() → clears localStorage → redirects to login
end note

note over API
  JWKS cached as module-level global in security.py.
  Cache miss → re-fetch from Cognito's .well-known/jwks.json endpoint.
end note

@enduml
